  "effect.monsterexpansion.discombobulated.guidebook_description": "Makes you unable to move nor attack for a short duration. This status is very common and can be inflicted by most monsters' roars. However as common as it is, the monsters also do not attack when roaring, making the status not as dangerous. As the effect will likely end before the monster can finish roaring.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.stunned.guidebook_description": "Makes you unable to move nor attack for a short duration. This can be inflicted by all monsters if the hunter is often hit by attacks. The effect instantly ends if the hunter is hit again. The damage source does not matter, making allies and self-inflicted damage a viable way to end the effect early. However this effect is still very dangerous as the monster may follow up with a devastating attack before the hunter can recover.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.bleeding.guidebook_description": "Makes you take damage over time. This effect can stack, making the damage interval shorter. On its own, the damage isn't anything to be afraid of, but it can be devastating if its allowed to stack up. This status' duration will go down slower depending on how fast you are moving. To get rid of it the fastest, the hunter must crouch while staying still.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.flarevein.guidebook_description": "Makes you take damage over time. This effect can stack, making the damage interval shorter. On its own, the damage isn't anything to be afraid of, but it can be devastating if its allowed to stack up. This status' duration will go down slower depending on how slow you are moving. To get rid of it the fastest, the hunter must be sprinting, or even better, roll around until the status is cured. The hunter must be careful as to not stay still, as doing so will increase the duration instead.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.frostvein.guidebook_description": "Makes you move slower, attack slower and jump lower. This effect can stack, making the movement speed decrease more severe. This effect can really be devastating if its allowed to stack up as you may not be able to jump over even a singular block. This status currently does not have a remedy making it incredibly dangerous if the hunter is fighting in rough terrain.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.remedy.no_remedy": "No Remedy",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.remedy.dont_move": "Dont move.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.remedy.crouch": "Crouch.",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.remedy.sprint": "Sprint",
  "effect.monsterexpansion.remedy.roll": "Roll."
 }
